{"task_id": "HumanEval/24", "solution": "def largest_divisor(n: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\" For a given number n, find the largest number that divides n evenly, smaller than n\n    \"\"\"\n    # Iterate from n // 2 down to 1 to find the largest divisor.\n    for i in range(n // 2, 0, -1):\n        if n % i == 0:\n            return i\n    return 1 # This line is theoretically unreachable for n > 1 as 1 is always a divisor."}
{"task_id": "HumanEval/25", "solution": "def factorize(n: int) -> List[int]:\n    \"\"\" Return list of prime factors of given integer in the order from smallest to largest.\n    Each of the factors should be listed number of times corresponding to how many times it appeares in factorization.\n    \"\"\"\n    factors = []\n    d = 2\n    temp_n = n\n\n    while d * d <= temp_n:\n        while temp_n % d == 0:\n            factors.append(d)\n            temp_n //= d\n        d += 1\n\n    if temp_n > 1:\n        factors.append(temp_n)\n    \n    return factors"}
